    {
      "op": "replace_text",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/9/argument/0/text",
      "old": "Fix a smooth exact twisted path v on [0,T] and its numerical interpolation V with residual Rres.",
      "new": "Fix any smooth real mean-zero solution u of u_t+u_xxx=(1/2)*partial_x(u^2) on [0,T], the normalized KdV equation of D020, and define v(t)=S_(-t)u(t). Take its numerical interpolation V with residual Rres."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace_text",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/9/argument/0/text",
      "old": "Differentiating the twisted exact equation gives v'=B(v,v)/2. Subtract N007 to get e'=B_t(e,v-e/2)-Rres'.",
      "new": "For the exact path, D004 gives partial_t S_(-t)=partial_x^3 S_(-t), commuting with spatial derivatives. Thus v'=S_(-t)(u_t+u_xxx)=(1/2)S_(-t)partial_x(u^2)=(1/2)B_t(v,v), since S_t v=u. Smoothness justifies this differentiation and the spatial products. Subtracting N007's identity V'=B_t(V,V)/2+Rres' and using symmetry and bilinearity gives e'=(B_t(v,v)-B_t(V,V))/2-Rres'=B_t(e,(v+V)/2)-Rres'=B_t(e,v-e/2)-Rres'."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace_text",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/10/argument/0/text",
      "old": "Use N010 with a constant C_M enlarged to work throughout this ball.",
      "new": "N001 identifies u as a smooth solution of u_t+u_xxx=u*u_x=(1/2)*partial_x(u^2) and v=S_(-t)u, so the explicit normalized exact-solution premise of N010 is satisfied. Use N010 with a constant C_M enlarged to work throughout this ball."
    },
